  "notes": "{甘受|かんじゅ} means accepting something unpleasant without resistance. It implies resignation or willingness to endure hardship.\n\nWRITING:\nThe character {甘|かん} here means \"willingly\" or \"contentedly,\" not its more common meaning of \"sweet.\"\n\nCOMMON OBJECTS (always negative):\n- {批判|ひはん}を{甘受|かんじゅ}する: to accept criticism\n- {処分|しょぶん}を{甘受|かんじゅ}する: to accept punishment\n- {不利益|ふりえき}を{甘受|かんじゅ}する: to accept disadvantage\n- {結果|けっか}を{甘受|かんじゅ}する: to accept consequences\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {受|う}け{入|い}れる: to accept (neutral; broader use)\n- {我慢|がまん}する: to endure, put up with (focuses on the suffering)\n- {諦|あきら}める: to give up, resign oneself (focuses on abandoning hope)\n\nREGISTER:\nFormal and literary. Common in written Japanese, legal contexts, and serious discussion. Rarely used in casual conversation.",
